\begin_layout Subsection
The Dataset Employed
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
In this study,
 we utilized a large-scale dataset of historical football matches sourced from a professional sports analytics repository.
 The data collection process prioritized high granularity,
 incorporating not only match results but also advanced performance indicators and pre-match market probabilities.
 The dataset's reliability is ensured through its internal consistency and widespread use in sports forecasting benchmarks.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Dataset Description
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The experimental dataset comprises 225,474 match events spanning from 2018 to 2026.
 To ensure rigorous evaluation,
 the data was partitioned into a training set of 149,998 matches and a dedicated test set of 75,476 matches.
